  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Theilenhofen</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Roman fort at Theilenhofen, called Iciniacum in antiquity, was a Roman military camp along the Upper Germanic-Raetian Limes. The site lies to the northwest of the village of Theilenhofen in the Wei\u00dfenburg-Gunzenhausen district of Bavaria. The fort was probably built in the middle of the third century CE.",
